<title>GREECE: Greek M3 rose provisionally 7.8 pct yr/yr in Nov.</title>
<headline>Greek M3 rose provisionally 7.8 pct yr/yr in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek M3 money supply rose provisionally 7.8 percent year-on-year in November from a revised 8.6 percent in October, within the central bank's 6.0-9.0 percent target range for end-96, the Bank of Greece said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The M4 monetary aggregate grew provisionally 11.1 percent year-on-year in November after a revised 10.5 percent rise in October, it said.</p>
<p>    M3 money supply	 Nov 96*   Oct 96**   Nov 95</p>
<p>    Stock (bln drachs)   17,077.6  17,050.4   15,847.8</p>
<p>    Yr-on-year		  7.8	8.6	  10.3</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
